#text("The outstanding target is skipped_256_876-twist2: a 512-bit degree-2 extension-twist order associated with P-256 candidate 876. It is not the 256-bit base-field curve order or its base-field quadratic-twist order. Its certified partition remains 1657 × 45294121 × 5333949541 × C, where C is the exact 444-bit composite in the ")#link("https://github.com/isogeny-labs/crypto/blob/ba09a5e482f0a8faa7fac0ec76c1ed5ce029c4b2/research/nist_skipped_curve_dissection_20261021/factorization/rounds/R08-20261025/result.json")[#text("result")]#text(". The ")#link("https://github.com/isogeny-labs/crypto/blob/ba09a5e482f0a8faa7fac0ec76c1ed5ce029c4b2/research/nist_skipped_curve_dissection_20261021/factorization/README.md")[#text("factorization scope")]#text(" explains the imported timeout fields. Resolving these arithmetic fields does not establish why a seed was historically skipped.")

#heading(level: 2)[#text("What the relation counts mean")]

#text("A raw NFS relation is a recorded arithmetic relation produced by sieving. It is input to later processing. Rows can repeat, fail an integrity check, or fail to combine into the dependencies needed for linear algebra. More raw rows are more collected data; they are not discovered prime factors.")

