#text("An ideal appearing in only one remaining relation cannot cancel in a dependency. Removing its relation can expose another singleton, so pruning cascades. Here the filter tracked ideals above its cutoff of 100,000 and ended with 0 tracked large ideals. That does not mean the entire integer factorization was solved. The native controller requested more relations; rank and a usable matrix were not established.")

#text("The 92 count applies to the older 4.59-million-row input. The newer 10.44-million-row checkpoint has not been filtered. Applying the old survival fraction to the new file would be an unsupported extrapolation.")

